<title>USA: Sikorsky says lays off 80 in Connecticut.</title>
<headline>Sikorsky says lays off 80 in Connecticut.</headline>
<dateline>STRATFORD, Conn. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Helicopter maker Sikorsky Aircraft Corp., a unit of United Technologies Corp., said Thursday it had laid off 80 salaried employees because of a shrinking U.S. defense procurement.</p>
<p>&quot;The reason is decreased procurement of Sikorsky helicopters by the U.S. government,&quot; Sikorsky spokesman Bill Tuttle told Reuters. &quot;This has been going on for a few years.&quot;</p>
<p>Tuttle declined to comment on whether any more layoffs were anticipated.</p>
<p>Sikorsky's workforce has shrunk to 8,500 from more than 12,000 in the late 1980s.</p>
<p>&quot;Its been declining steadily, in keeping with the amount of production,&quot; Tuttle said.</p>
<p>Most of the company's employees are in Connecticut. It also has a flight test facility in West Palm Beach, Fla., and field-service personnel in overseas locations.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224</p>
